# Story: As a terminal planner, I want each container to have at most one open booking, so that two trucks are never sent for the same container. If a container already has a booking that is BOOKED, another booking for it (by anyone, for any slot) is refused with DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING. After the first booking is cancelled the container can be booked again.

@draft

Feature: Container Booking Rules

Scenario Outline: Book a container (with value table)
  Given I am a driver
  And the slot has <slot_capacity> places left
  When I book that slot for a valid container
  Then the booking is confirmed with a reference
  And the slot has <remaining_places> place(s) left

Examples:
| slot_capacity | remaining_places |
| 2              | 1               |
| 1              | 0               |

Scenario: Booking Refused Due to DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING
  Given I am a driver
  When another driver books a different slot for the same container
  Then their booking is refused because "DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING"

Scenario: Canceling a Booking
  Given my booking has been cancelled
  And the slot has <slot_capacity> places left
  When I cancel my booking
  Then the outcome is <outcome>

Scenario: Change Slot Refused Due to CHANGE_CUTOFF_PASSED
  Given another driver has booked that slot
  When a clerk checks the truck in
  Then the change is refused because "CHANGE_CUTOFF_PASSED"

Scenario: Check-In Refused Because FORBIDDEN
  Given I am a driver
  And my booking has been checked in
  When I try to check myself in
  Then the check-in is refused because "FORBIDDEN"

Scenario: Booking on Gate Screen
  Given another driver has booked that slot
  When a clerk checks the truck in
  Then the gate screen shows the booking as checked in
